cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  pyDADA2 is an unofficial Python port of the DADA2 R package by Benjamin Callahan, Paul McMurdie,
  Susan Holmes and the DADA2 contributors. All credit for the method and its implementation goes
  to them: if you use pyDADA2, please cite the DADA2 paper (preferred-citation below), not this
  port, plus the papers listed under references when they apply (PacBio error model, taxonomy
  classifier). The port itself was made with extensive AI assistance to fit Python workflows.
title: "pyDADA2: a Python port of DADA2"
abstract: >-
  Unofficial Python port of DADA2 1.36 (exact amplicon sequence variant inference). It reuses
  DADA2's C++ core, moves performance-critical R code to C++ and exposes a scikit-learn-style API.
  Validated against the R package. The method and its implementation are the work of the DADA2
  authors (preferred-citation and references below); the author listed here only made the port.
type: software
